          "text": "Clinical Indication  \nDrug-resistant focal epilepsy of infectious etiology, with focal impaired-awareness seizures beginning at age 12 and occurring approximately four times per month. Current antiseizure medications are oxcarbazepine and zonisamide.\n\nTechnique  \nRoutine digital scalp EEG performed using the international 10–20 electrode placement system.\n\nFindings  \nNo authorized background, interictal, or ictal EEG findings were provided; therefore, no specific electrographic findings are described.\n\nImpression  \nIndeterminate routine EEG interpretation in the absence of authorized tracing findings. No EEG-based conclusion regarding epileptiform abnormalities, seizure occurrence, or localization can be made.",
